        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-13T11:30:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It feels strange to get the icon once just to see if notifications should be enabled, then possibly get the icon to show from a different array.\n\nHow about having the methods return a boolean indicating whether this type of notification was enabled (and shown) ?\nThen something like:\n\nif ((mNetworkSuspended \u0026\u0026 setupPauseNotification())\n    || (mConnectedClients \u003e 0 \u0026\u0026 setupHotspotClientsNotification())\n    || setupNotification()) {\n  return;\n}\nclearNotification();\n\nEach method would return false when iconArray.length() \u003c 1, so no need to check for the size of tethering_notification_icons.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 150,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 158,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "c1feb0c3c9b05e274dfd0ab42f508e692a0c2756",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
